From e524349cc85e7db026680a247cd5f734e6a088ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 08:23:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ggml-cpu): read the experts from a copy local to each
 node

The gpu backend binds to node 0, and its CPU expert reads (74% of a
4-token verify step) use one socket's memory bandwidth. koishi has a
second copy of the model files whose page cache is mostly on node 1.

- LLAMA_NUMA_MIRROR=node:from=to[,...] maps the copy of each model file
  (the same path under `to`) a second time, and registers the still
  mapped fragments with the CPU backend (ggml_numa_mirror_set / clear,
  through the CPU backend's proc address table). No new memory: the
  copy is the page cache another process already holds.
- A thread whose CPUs are all on one node (--numa distribute, isolate,
  or numactl bound to one node) records that node. MUL_MAT_ID (vec_dot,
  sgemm and the fused small-batch MoE op) reads an expert's rows from
  the copy of that node.
- With --numa distribute (thread ith on node ith % n_nodes) the fused
  MoE op splits its units into one contiguous part per node, each with
  its own counter, so no counter moves between sockets.

Each output is the same vec_dot over the same bytes, by another thread,
so the result is exact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6MCJC4HTKxvuGjKjqDuqQ
